{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2d0-7ac7-7f03-8c97-ccb0ee9decb3"},"sequence":67,"recorded_at":1780531400000129,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b2d0-a74e-77d3-9e1b-e4dda1c027d7"},"task_id":"01a0b2d0-a74e-77d3-9e1b-e4dda1c027d7","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b2d0-a74e-77d3-9e1b-e4dda1c027d7","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2g5be6/TASK-260830-2g5be6_rework-rev3.md`.\n1|THIS BRIEF SUPERSEDES EVERY EARLIER PRECONDITION ON TASK-260830-2g5be6, including TASK-260830-2g5be6_rework-rev2.md. Do exactly what is written here.\n2|Rework run for TASK-260830-2g5be6 (implement-native-capture-and-source-race-check, SECOND leaf of STORY-260830-1cyj0q). Change Request revision 2 was reviewed by RUN-260918-fdce92 (claude-opus-5 max) and routed CHANGES REQUESTED — but read the first paragraph of TASK-260830-2g5be6_review-verdict-rev2.md before anything else, because almost everything is now closed: all five rev1 survivors are KILLED 2/2 on your tree, the three inherited advisories carry explicit dispositions, the P3 prose-and-rows items are fixed, and production is still correct on all 36 new probe lines the reviewer drove — no admit-hole, no containment escape, no behaviour-changing fork of a landed gate. Do not touch any of that.\n3|What blocks acceptance is two AC rows, and the same shape as last time: your results, matrix and LOGBOOK restate \"17 of 17 AC rows measured at the member level — every row's narrowing reddens its killer\", and the reviewer measures **15 of 17**. Two rows name a member their committed test never reaches, so a narrowing SURVIVES the whole suite twice while the row's tests stay green and the admitted behaviour was executed under the plant.\n4|1. **Row 8** — the `unstable_archive` boundary's pre/post digests. In `TestCaptureArchiveSealsUnstable`, assert the SEALED boundary's `pre_capture_digest == result.PreDigest` and `post_capture_digest == result.PostDigest` (decode `CaptureBoundary.Pre/PostCaptureDigest`, or match the literal strings in the sealed bytes), and assert the sealed generation equals the request generation. Ship a harness row of the `R2-unstable-seals-pre-as-post` shape.\n5|2. **Row 10** — \"before any seal\" is pinned at `Capture` but not at `CaptureAndProject`. In `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt`, scan the CAPTURE store for any decodable raw or capture manifest, the way `TestCaptureRaceSealsNoManifest` already does. Ship a harness row of the `R2-project-seal-before-gate` shape (seal first, gate second, race error preserved) and note in the row that `N-race-order-project` is killed by the seal error message.\n6|3. P3-a: one committed row with an UNPLANNED special member (a symlink to an outside file, optionally a FIFO) refusing \"not a plan candidate\" and naming the member, with no outside bytes installed; harness row of the `R2-unplanned-special-admitted` shape.\n7|4. P3-b: `TestCaptureRefusesSymlinkedStoreRoot` — the refusal names the link and nothing is installed; harness row of the `R2-store-root-follows-symlink` shape (a narrowing keyed on the link name is fine).\n8|5. P3-c: one race row where the EXCLUDED member's size changes at post, refusing and naming `store/token-cache`, with a harness row of the `R2-excluded-size-ignored` shape — or reword the TRACEABILITY and results bound to \"presence and shape changes still race\". Either is acceptable; say which you chose.\n9|6. P3-d/e: state in TRACEABILITY that the branch bound's measured gate is the landed `DecodeWorkspaceBinding` and that the local check is defence in depth, plus whatever the verdict's item 6 names.\n10|And the number itself: publish the ratio you MEASURE after these rows land, with each row's killer named. Restating 17 of 17 is what produced this round; if two rows are still unmeasured after your changes, say 15 of 17 and name them — an honest smaller number is accepted, an inflated one is a finding.\n11|Procedure: your candidate is on a base carrying a12d1bd; current origin/main is c3aae73. Do not refresh unless origin/main actually moves; if it does, run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2g5be6` and audit every path in `git diff --name-only <old base> <new base>` that also appears in your `git status`, keeping README/LOGBOOK edits additive on the NEW content. You are a MIDDLE leaf: do NOT touch internal/traceability. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. Re-run the full configured validation suite once (30 commands at trunk c3aae73 — read the count from the candidate config; command 5 is the race gate with `-timeout 25m` and can take 25-40 minutes under concurrent runs). Update the results with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update the conformance matrix and the evidence archive (a real gzip archive, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1), re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-2g5be6 --role developer` so revision 3 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 2 hours in — this is two assertions, four harness rows and a number.\n12|PARTIAL-ATTEMPT RECOVERY: if a previous attempt died to a provider idle timeout, the Story worktree still carries its partial edits — start with `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree status --short` and `git diff`, state what you inherited, and verify it against this brief instead of assuming it is correct.\n13|Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-s