{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c61d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2d0-7ac7-7f03-8c97-ccb0ee9decb3"},"sequence":361,"recorded_at":1780531400000717,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2"},"call_id":"call_01a0b2d1af8b707ba1c299f917ce5431","text":"Read text file `/tmp/t2g5/verdict-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2g5be6 — Review verdict, Change Request revision 2\n2|\n3|Reviewer run: RUN-260918-fdce92 (claude-opus-5 max, reviewer/reviewer).\n4|Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-2g5be6-2` revision 2, base\n5|`2f844bb49702a860c1199a6a2a0ca6a5cc878197` (the predecessor's checkpoint on the\n6|Story branch), candidate tree `e7c9a12d1cd487e7697ef3b33f71430ef65f136a` (22\n7|paths; patch sha256 `c0a19165154358956450a216e3702ad7dda76f227ff3afb030e47ba1dec5de37`,\n8|verified equal to `git diff 2f844bb e7c9a12d`). The live Story worktree's\n9|temp-index tree OID (`git read-tree HEAD && git add -A` into a scratch index)\n10|equalled `e7c9a12d…` before this review and `git status` stayed\n11|` M LOGBOOK.md`, ` M README.md`, `?? internal/clonesnap/`; the worktree, index,\n12|branch and HEAD were never touched. `origin/main` is still `c3aae73`\n13|(unchanged since the rework spawn; no refresh was due).\n14|Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §13.14.1 (lines 10331–10546),\n15|§10.2 (4851–4900), §7.8 (3738–3925), re-extracted and diffed member-for-member\n16|against the candidate. (As in rev1, the reviewer brief's \"Section 4.C /\n17|terminalbackend\" paragraph is a copy from another leaf; this review covers the\n18|capture scope the task and producer brief define.)\n19|\n20|## Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED → `to-dev`\n21|\n22|Revision 2 closes everything revision 1 asked for: all five rev1 survivors are\n23|KILLED 2/2 on the new tree (section 0), the three inherited advisories carry an\n24|explicit disposition, the P3-γ/δ/ε′/ζ′ prose-and-rows items are fixed, and\n25|production is still correct on every probe I drove (36 new probe lines, no\n26|admit-hole, no containment escape, no fork of a landed gate that changes\n27|behaviour). What blocks acceptance is, once more and more narrowly, the\n28|evidence contract: the results, matrix and LOGBOOK restate **\"17 of 17 AC rows\n29|measured at the member level — every row's narrowing reddens its killer\"**,\n30|and I measure **15 of 17**. Two AC rows carry a named member whose committed\n31|test does not reach it — a narrowing SURVIVES the whole committed suite 2/2\n32|while the row's tests stay green, and the admitted behaviour was executed\n33|under the plant:\n34|\n35|- **Row 8** — the `unstable_archive` form's `pre/post digests`: the sealed\n36|  archive manifest can carry the PRE digest for `post_capture_digest` (equal\n37|  digests while flagged `source_not_quiescent`) and `TestCaptureArchiveSealsUnstable`\n38|  stays green; it asserts the RESULT's measured digests, never the sealed ones.\n39|- **Row 10** — \"Mutation check runs before any seal or projection output\" at\n40|  `CaptureAndProject`: the projection entry can seal and PUBLISH the raw\n41|  manifest before the race gate and still return the race refusal;\n42|  `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt` stays green because it inspects only the\n43|  target sink and the error text. The shipped `N-race-order-project` row is\n44|  killed by the *seal error message* (the landed builder refusing unequal\n45|  digests), not by a sink assertion; the `RacePolicy` doc contract \"RaceRefuse\n46|  aborts capture with no sealed manifest\" is unpinned at that entry.\n47|\n48|Both are one assertion plus one harness row each. Three more surviving plants\n49|(P3) name sub-classes with no committed row at all (an unplanned SPECIAL\n50|member, a symlinked store root, an EXCLUDED member's size change — the last\n51|one a TRACEABILITY claim stated as fact). The rework is precise and small\n52|(section \"Rework scope\").\n53|\n54|Method: isolated immutable copies of the exact candidate tree (`git archive\n55|e7c9a12d…` → `.temp/TASK-260830-2g5be6/rev2-review/{pristine,candidate}`,\n56|`.task-board` artifact dropped; `diff -rq` clean against `pristine` before use\n57|and after every battery, probe and hygiene run). Every probe and plant drove a\n58|production entry (`Capture`, `CaptureAndProject`, `AdmitForTarget`,\n59|`CheckpointWorkspace`); `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` for every harness, zero\n60|`__pycache__`/`.pyc` in any copy or in the candidate tree. Raw evidence:\n61|`TASK-260830-2g5be6_review-evidence-rev2.tar.gz` (`logs/`, one raw `go test`\n62|log per plant per run under `logs/mutants/run{1,2}/` (20 each) and\n63|`logs/mutants-producer/run{1,2}/` (35 each), `logs/under-mutant/` executions\n64|of each survivor, `reviewer_mutants_rev2.py`, `run_under_mutant.py`, the three\n65|probe files as `.txt`, `logs/probes-rev2.log` with 36 `PROBE` lines,\n66|`logs/crash-rev2.log`, `MANIFEST.sha256`).\n67|\n68|## 0. Rework verification (rev1 findings against the NEW tree)\n69|\n70|| rev1 finding | rev2 change | re-plant (whole suite, 2 runs) | Verdict |\n71||---|---|---|---|\n72|| P2-α row 14 (§10.2 MUST, no test looked at a payload blob) | `TestCaptureInstallsEveryPayloadBlob` + `assertEveryRawBlobInstalled` in the crash replay | `R1-skip-payload-install-blob-b` **KILLED 2/2** (killers: `TestCaptureInstallsEveryPayloadBlob`, `TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates`) | closed |\n73|| P2-α row 8 (target sink never inspected on the archive path) | `TestProjectRefusesUnstable` keeps its sink and asserts zero blobs | `R1-archive-emits-receipt` **KILLED 2/2** | closed |\n74|| P2-α row 2 (every symlink/FIFO row `Required: true`) | `TestCaptureRefusesOptionalSymlinkedIntermediate`, `TestCaptureRefusesOptionalFIFO` | `R1-blockedAncestor-optional` **KILLED 2/2** | closed |\n75|| P2-α row 9 (unreadable-at-post class had no row) | `TestCaptureRaceUnreadableAtPost` (grown past `MaxSingleBytes`) | `R1-post-falls-back-to-captured-hash` **KILLED 2/2**; my chmod-000 member of the class also refuses on pristine (probe P8) | closed |\n76|| P2-α row 5 / P3-ε (excluded unknown unpinned) | `TestCaptureOptionalAbsentUnknownMakesRawIncomplete` | `R1-clonebundle-unknown-ignores-excluded` **KILLED 2/2**; through `CaptureAndProject(maximal_safe)` proper the excluded unknown refuses with an empty target sink (probe P11a) | closed |\n77|| P2-β inherited advisories silent | results §\"Inherited advisories\": ε CLOSED (test + cross-package row), ζ DEFERRED to TASK-260830-32ypr2 with reason, η PARTIAL (entry re-validation pinned by `TestCaptureRefusesInvalidSourceIdentity`; standalone contract deferred) | dispositions verified against the tree; the `CaptureRequest.SourceIdentity` doc now states the re-validation | closed |\n78|| P3-γ false \"fail closed under a reorder\" justification | seals `state.post` for `post_capture_digest`; bound reworded in all four places; `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt` asserts the race literal | sealed post == measured post on both paths (probe P10a/P10b); `C-stable-seals-pre-as-post` SURVIVED as an equivalence control must | closed (but see P2-α row 10 for what the new killer actually measures) |\n79|| P3-δ `N-workspace-cwd` message-keyed | row note reworded as defence-in-depth | reproduced KILLED 2/2, note honest | closed |\n80|| P3-ε′ leak rows killed by the builder, not the scan | `N-excluded-orphan-blob` add-write shipped | reproduced KILLED 2/2 by `TestCaptureExcludesSecrets`'s blob scan | closed |\n81|| P3-ζ′ fidelity vocabulary spelled twice | recorded as a bound in `project.go`, TRACEABILITY, matrix, results | present | closed (bound) |\n82|\n83|Also re-run from rev1: `R1-size-equality-is-proof` (widening) KILLED 2/2 by 7\n84|tests; `R1-hook-after-post-measure` (seam control) KILLED 2/2 by 12 tests.\n85|\n86|## Findings\n87|\n88|No P1.\n89|\n90|### P2 — evidence contract (claimed member-level ratio is inflated)\n91|\n92|- **P2-α \"17 of 17 measured at the member level\" is 15 of 17.** Two rows name\n93|  a member their tests do not reach; each plant SURVIVED the whole committed\n94|  suite in two independent runs (`logs/mutants/run{1,2}/`) and its admitted\n95|  behaviour was executed under the plant (`logs/under-mutant/`):\n96|  - **Row 8 \"unstable_archive carries generation, pre/post digests, …\"** —\n97|    `R2-unstable-seals-pre-as-post` (the unstable `BoundaryInput` seals\n98|    `state.pre` for `PostCaptureDigest`, `capture.go:482`) **SURVIVED 2/2**.\n99|    Under it (`logs/under-mutant/R2-unstable-seals-pre-as-post.log`, probe U5):\n100|    `kind=unstable_archive`, measured `pre != post` true, **sealed pre == sealed\n101|    post true, sealed post == measured post false** — the archive manifest\n102|    misrepresents the post-capture state while `TestCaptureArchiveSealsUnstable`,\n103|    `TestCaptureArchiveRequiresExplicit`, `TestProjectRefusesUnstable/Direct`\n104|    all PASS. The test asserts the literal `kind`/`reason_code`/\n105|    `operator_explicit`/`target_projection_forbidden` members and\n106|    `result.PreDigest != result.PostDigest` (the pipeline's measurement, not\n107|    the seal); the generation is pinned only indirectly through `N-g2`. The\n108|    §7.8 `capture` response and §13.14.1 name these two digests as the\n109|    evidence the form exists to carry. Pristine seals the two measured digests\n110|    (probe P10b).\n111|  - **Row 10 \"Mutation check runs before any seal or projection output —\n112|    `Capture`, `CaptureAndProject` (ORDER-PIN)\"** — `R2-project-seal-before-gate`\n113|    (`CaptureAndProject` calls `sealAndPublish(false)` first, then the race\n114|    gate, and returns the race refusal; the stable capture-manifest seal fails\n115|    closed on unequal digests so no receipt can be emitted) **SURVIVED 2/2**.\n116|    Under it (`logs/under-mutant/R2-project-seal-before-gate.log`, probe U1): a\n117|    race under `RaceRefuse` through the projection entry returns the race\n118|    refusal with **`raw_manifests=1`** published in the capture store\n119|    (pristine: 0) — `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt` PASSES (race literal\n120|    present, target sink empty). The same shape at the `Capture` entry,\n121|    `R2-capture-seal-before-gate`, is KILLED 2/2 by `TestCaptureRaceSealsNoManifest`'s\n122|    store scan, so the rule is pinned on one of the two named call sites only\n123|    (the rev1 brief's shape (b)). The shipped `N-race-order-project` row is\n124|    killed by `race_test.go:220: refusal \"… stable snapshot proof: … capture\n125|    digests differ …\" misses \"source mutated during capture\"` — the seal\n126|    error message, not a sink; its note's \"and on any emitted receipt blob\" is\n127|    inert because under that plant no receipt is ever emitted. The `RacePolicy`\n128|    doc (\"RaceRefuse aborts capture with no sealed manifest\") and the\n129|    `CaptureAndProject` doc (\"no projection output is produced before the race\n130|    is decided\") are therefore pinned only for the receipt, not for the seal,\n131|    at the projection entry.\n132|\n133|### P3 — sub-classes with no committed row; prose that outruns the tests\n134|\n135|- **P3-a Unplanned SPECIAL members are unmeasured.** `R2-unplanned-special-admitted`\n136|  (`intermediatePrefix` treats exactly one unplanned symlink `stray-link` as\n137|  an intermediate, `walk.go:220`) **SURVIVED 2/2**. Under it (probe U2) an\n138|  unplanned symlink to an outside secret is silently dropped and the capture\n139|  seals **`stable`, `raw_complete=true`** (no outside byte leaks — the special\n140|  is never opened). Pristine refuses `capture store member \"stray-link\" is not\n141|  a plan candidate` (probe P1; unplanned FIFO likewise, P2). Every committed\n142|  unplanned row (`zz-extra`, `blob-a-evil`) is a regular file, so the matrix\n143|  row 3 / TRACEABILITY \"Unplanned members refuse\" holds for regular files only.\n144|- **P3-b A symlinked STORE root has no committed test.** `R2-store-root-follows-symlink`\n145|  (`OpenNoFollowDir` → `os.Open` at `capture.go:201`; widening, labelled) **SURVIVED\n146|  2/2**; under it a symlinked root captures successfully (probe U3). Pristine\n147|  refuses `secprim unsafe path: target symlink: link-root` (probe P4).\n148|  `TestCheckpointWorkspaceRefusesSymlinkRoot` pins the workspace root; nothing\n149|  pins the store root that row 2 \"capture never escapes the store root\" rests\n150|  on.\n151|- **P3-c TRACEABILITY \"presence, shape, and size changes still race\" (for\n152|  excluded members) is a claim without a test.** `R2-excluded-size-ignored`\n153|  (exactly `store/token-cache` contributes a constant size to the source\n154|  record, `capture.go:347`) **SURVIVED 2/2**; under it the credential member's\n155|  size change seals `stable` silently (probe U4). Pristine refuses naming\n156|  `store/token-cache` (probe P9b). Every committed race row mutates an\n157|  INCLUDED member or adds/removes a file. Either ship the row or state the\n158|  bound as \"presence and shape\".\n159|- **P3-d `workspaceNullableText` is defence in depth, credited as the gate.**\n160|  `R2-branch-1025` (`length > maximum+1`) **SURVIVED 2/2**: the 1025-character\n161|  branch is refused by the landed `DecodeWorkspaceBinding` (`identity.go:238`,\n162|  same literal `string[1..1024]`), so `TestCheckpointWorkspaceMultibyteBranch`\n163|  stays green (probe U6: `sealed workspace binding refused: … branch is not a\n164|  string[1..1024]`). Production correct; the TRACEABILITY row \"1.6 string\n165|  measure in characters | `workspaceNullableText` via `environ.StringLength`\"\n166|  attributes the kill to the local check. State it (the fingerprint-count\n167|  bound is different: `R2-fingerprints-129` is KILLED by the local literal\n168|  \"maximum is 128\").\n169|- **P3-e Harness census.** Beyond the rows above, the shipped harness carries\n170|  no row for the plan member-grammar gate (`R2-plan-grammar-admits-dotdot`\n171|  KILLED 2/2 by `TestCaptureRefusesParentPlanKey` — `SanitizeNativeKey` admits\n172|  `..`, so `CheckMemberPath` at `walk.go:141` is the only gate), the required\n173|  branch's `blockedAncestor` (`R2-required-blockedAncestor-dropped` KILLED\n174|  2/2, message-keyed on \"symlink\"), the fingerprint count and the chunk size\n175|  bound (`R2-first-chunk-oversize` KILLED 2/2). All pinned; add them or state\n176|  them.\n177|\n178|### Informational (no action required unless cheap)\n179|\n180|- `AdmitForTarget` admits a sealed capture manifest with trailing JSON\n181|  whitespace (`…}\\n`, probe P6b `err=<nil>`); non-whitespace trailing data,\n182|  raw-as-capture, empty, truncated and a forged `raw_complete:true` beside an\n183|  unknown item all refuse (P6a/c/d/e). This is the landed strict decoder's\n184|  frame rule (\"trailing data\" = non-whitespace) — clonebundle owner's call,\n185|  not this leaf's.\n186|- Nil `TargetSink` refuses before any capture (probe P3, store empty) — no\n187|  committed test, trivial.\n188|- A store subdirectory made unreadable at post time refuses with the\n189|  enumeration error, not the race literal, and never archives (probe P9d,\n190|  archive policy) — acceptable under \"refusal or unstable_archive\"; worth a\n191|  line.\n192|- Seal-time refusals still leave payload blobs as content-addressed orphans\n193|  (rev1 informational; unchanged).\n194|\n195|## What is clean (verified, not read)\n196|\n197|1. **Spec fidelity** (`logs/probes-rev2.log`): the nine-class vocabulary and\n198|   always-excluded four; included/excluded content rule; `plan_optional_absent`;\n199|   excluded unknown → `raw_complete=false` and `maximal_safe` refused through\n200|   `CaptureAndProject` (P11a) while `strict_exact` admits (P11b); stable proof\n201|   digests sealed equal to the measurement on both paths (P10a/b); the archive\n202|   raw manifest carries the pre-mutation bytes (P10c); plan-key grammar\n203|   refuses `..`, `./`, `//`, trailing `/`, `.`, `store/./x`, backslash and\n204|   `%2e%2e` for OPTIONAL keys too, before any install (P7); empty plan over an\n205|   empty store seals 0 entries, `raw_complete=true`, spec-consistent (P16);\n206|   required-ness of an excluded class is inert (P17, matches the stated\n207|   bound).\n208|2. **Containment**: symlinked intermediate (required and optional), trailing\n209|   symlink, FIFO (required and optional), directory member, excluded symlink\n210|   to an outside secret never followed (P13a `leaked=false`), symlinked store\n211|   root refused, relative store root refused (P5), backslash-named member\n212|   refused (P12). Producer rows `N-contain-*`, `N-fifo`, `N-optional-blocked-ancestor`\n213|   KILLED 2/2.\n214|3. **Exclusion**: `TestCaptureExcludesSecrets` scan is load-bearing\n215|   (`N-excluded-orphan-blob` KILLED 2/2); no secret in blob, manifest, log or\n216|   error.\n217|4. **Source race**: changed byte at equal size, changed size, appended\n218|   record, replaced file, removed file, grown-past-bound, chmod 000 (P8),\n219|   retype to a same-content symlink (P9), excluded member size change (P9b)\n220|   all refuse naming the member; excluded equal-size content change seals\n221|   stable (P9c — the stated bound, confirmed); `R1-size-equality-is-proof`\n222|   KILLED 2/2.\n223|5. **Ordering** at the `Capture` entry: `N-race-order-capture` and\n224|   `R2-capture-seal-before-gate` KILLED 2/2 by the store scan. At the\n225|   projection entry: pinned for the receipt (`N-race-order-project`, killed\n226|   by the seal error) — see P2-α row 10 for the seal half.\n227|6. **Crash/idempotency**: the producer's real-SIGKILL child at\n228|   `AfterRawPublish` reproduced 2/2 in the suite and 2/2 under `-count=2`;\n229|   my own SIGKILL at `AfterWalk` (`TestRev2CrashKillAfterWalk`, run twice,\n230|   `logs/crash-rev2.log`): 2 payload blobs, 0 manifests, **0 staged temp\n231|   files, 0 quarantine entries**; the replay installs both manifests\n232|   (`raw_installed=true capture_installed=true`, 4 blobs), every raw entry's\n233|   blob is present, and the replayed bytes are identical to a clean capture.\n234|   `TestProjectIsIdempotent` replay verifies-and-reuses every blob and the\n235|   receipt.\n236|7. **Blob discipline**: `N-payload-install-blob-b` KILLED 2/2 (every raw\n237|   entry's blob present after `Capture` and after the crash replay);\n238|   `N-descriptor-empty/offset`, `R2-first-chunk-oversize` KILLED 2/2; the\n239|   §10.2 example vector reproduced by the predecessor's rows stands.\n240|8. **Admission**: G2, maximal-safe, unknown-profile rows KILLED 2/2; forged\n241|   inputs refuse at the landed decoder (P6a/c/d/e).\n242|9. **Workspace**: 129 fingerprints refuse (`R2-fingerprints-129` KILLED),\n243|   duplicate/unsorted, escapes, sibling-prefix absolute cwd (P18c), empty cwd\n244|   (P18b) refuse; a symlink inside the root pointing outside seals\n245|   `cwd_relative=\"link\"` (P18a, lexically contained, rev1 informational).\n246|10. **Producer harness reproduced**: 34 KILLED + `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED,\n247|    twice, in the isolated copy (`logs/mutants-producer/run{1,2}/`, 35 raw\n248|    logs with `# exit=` each); tree `diff -rq` clean after each run.\n249|11. **Hygiene** (`logs/hygiene*.log`): `gofmt -l` empty over the whole tree;\n250|    `go vet ./...` exit 0; `go build ./...` exit 0; `GOOS=linux`/`GOOS=windows`\n251|    builds exit 0; `tracecheck` exit 0 (bindings=68, clauses 49/569 —\n252|    `internal/traceability` untouched); `cataloggen -adopted … -check` exit 0;\n253|    `git diff --check` clean on the worktree; package `-race` ok (0 DATA\n254|    RACE), cover 87.3%; neighbour suites (clonebundle, localstore, secprim,\n255|    canonicaljson, scalar, environ) ok; whole-repository `go test ./...\n256|    -count=1` 39/39 ok (`logs/repo-test.log` + `repo-test-specpin.log`; the\n257|    specpin package needs the tracked `.task-board` artifact I had dropped\n258|    from the copy and passes with it restored). Changed paths are exactly the\n259|    22 candidate paths; README and LOGBOOK purely additive (0 removed lines),\n260|    README makes no capability/CLI claim; LOGBOOK entry newest-first; the\n261|    producer evidence archive is a real gzip with 106 `MANIFEST.sha256` rows\n262|    all OK, no `__pycache__`, 35 per-plant logs per run with identical run1/\n263|    run2 verdicts; candidate `task-board.config.json` equals HEAD (27\n264|    commands; the CR validation log reports `required=30 green=30` against\n265|    the control root — accepted for the 25-minute race gate, which I did not\n266|    rerun; I ran `-race` on the package).\n267|\n268|## Reviewer mutation battery (`reviewer_mutants_rev2.py`, whole committed suite as killer, 2 runs, identical verdicts)\n269|\n270|| Row | Kind | Verdict | Killers |\n271||---|---|---|---|\n272|| R1-blockedAncestor-optional | narrowing | KILLED 2/2 | TestCaptureRefusesOptionalSymlinkedIntermediate |\n273|| R1-archive-emits-receipt | add-write | KILLED 2/2 | TestProjectRefusesUnstable |\n274|| R1-skip-payload-install-blob-b | narrowing | KILLED 2/2 | TestCaptureInstallsEveryPayloadBlob, TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates |\n275|| R1-post-falls-back-to-captured-hash | narrowing | KILLED 2/2 | TestCaptureRaceUnreadableAtPost |\n276|| R1-clonebundle-unknown-ignores-excluded | narrowing (inherited ε) | KILLED 2/2 | TestCaptureOptionalAbsentUnknownMakesRawIncomplete |\n277|| R1-size-equality-is-proof | widening | KILLED 2/2 | 7 tests |\n278|| R1-hook-after-post-measure | seam control | KILLED 2/2 | 12 tests |\n279|| R2-project-seal-before-gate | narrowing (ordering) | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P2-α row 10) |\n280|| R2-capture-seal-before-gate | narrowing (ordering, control) | KILLED 2/2 | TestCaptureRaceSealsNoManifest |\n281|| R2-unplanned-special-admitted | narrowing | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P3-a) |\n282|| R2-store-root-follows-symlink | widening (root only) | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P3-b) |\n283|| R2-excluded-size-ignored | narrowing | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P3-c) |\n284|| R2-unstable-seals-pre-as-post | narrowing | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P2-α row 8) |\n285|| R2-required-blockedAncestor-dropped | narrowing | KILLED 2/2 | TestCaptureRefusesSymlinkedIntermediate |\n286|| R2-plan-grammar-admits-dotdot | narrowing | KILLED 2/2 | TestCaptureRefusesParentPlanKey |\n287|| R2-fingerprints-129 | narrowing | KILLED 2/2 | TestCheckpointWorkspaceRefusesTooManyFingerprints |\n288|| R2-branch-1025 | narrowing | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P3-d, landed decoder is the gate) |\n289|| R2-first-chunk-oversize | narrowing | KILLED 2/2 | TestCaptureMultiChunkMember |\n290|| C-stable-seals-pre-as-post | equivalence control | SURVIVED 2/2 (expected) | — |\n291|| C-rev2-comment | harmless control | SURVIVED 2/2 (expected) | — |\n292|\n293|Measured ratio: 17 of 17 AC rows reached by a named test through a production\n294|entry; **15 of 17 closed at the member level** (rows 8 and 10 each carry a\n295|surviving narrowing on a member the row names, executed above); rows 2 and 3\n296|each carry an unmeasured sub-class (symlinked store root; unplanned special\n297|member) graded P3 because the row's stated members are pinned.\n298|\n299|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n300|\n301|1. Row 8: in `TestCaptureArchiveSealsUnstable` assert the SEALED boundary's\n302|   `pre_capture_digest == result.PreDigest` and `post_capture_digest ==\n303|   result.PostDigest` (decoded `CaptureBoundary.Pre/PostCaptureDigest` or the\n304|   literal strings in the sealed bytes) and that the sealed generation equals\n305|   the request generation; ship a harness row of the\n306|   `R2-unstable-seals-pre-as-post` shape.\n307|2. Row 10: in `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt` scan the CAPTURE store for any\n308|   decodable raw or capture manifest (as `TestCaptureRaceSealsNoManifest