{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c653","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2d0-7ac7-7f03-8c97-ccb0ee9decb3"},"sequence":388,"recorded_at":1780531400000771,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b2d1-bd9a-7571-af0a-50d273cf8462"},"task_id":"01a0b2d1-bd9a-7571-af0a-50d273cf8462","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b2d1-bd9a-7571-af0a-50d273cf8462","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/t2g5/results-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2g5be6 Results — implement-native-capture-and-source-race-check (rev2)\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story\n4|worktree (`task-board/story/STORY-260830-1cyj0q`) on the predecessor\n5|checkpoint `2f844bb` (Story branch over trunk `a12d1bd`); no commit\n6|on the Story branch. `origin/main` is `c3aae73` at handoff, unchanged\n7|since spawn, so no `refresh-candidate` ran.\n8|\n9|Revision 2 answers review RUN-260918-cee501 (CHANGES REQUESTED):\n10|production was correct on every probe; the rework closes the five\n11|AC rows whose cited tests did not reach the named member, records\n12|the three inherited advisories as closed/deferred with owners, and\n13|fixes the four prose-and-rows items. No production logic was\n14|rewritten except the P3-γ seal (measured post digest) and its\n15|documented consequence (the project ordering killer now also\n16|asserts the race refusal).\n17|\n18|## Delivered (rev1 scope, unchanged)\n19|\n20|`internal/clonesnap` implements the capture operation over a real\n21|on-disk provider store (second leaf of STORY-260830-1cyj0q):\n22|contained walk through the `secprim` Guard, nine-class\n23|classification with always-excluded bytes never opened, Capture\n24|Boundary from measured evidence, the source-race gate before any\n25|seal or projection output, workspace checkpoint + source head from\n26|observed state, Section 10.2 descriptors with `capability_unavailable`\n27|past 128 GiB, and target admission through the landed G2 and\n28|maximal-safe gates. Every artifact seals through the landed\n29|`clonebundle` builders and re-decodes before publish or return; no\n30|second model exists. No `ax` CLI, provider process, or network; no\n31|`internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin).\n32|\n33|## Finding-by-finding rework table (rev1 verdict → rev2 change)\n34|\n35|| Finding | Change | Test that fails without it | Evidence path |\n36||---|---|---|---|\n37|| P2-α Row 14 (§10.2 MUST; cited tests never looked at a payload blob) | New `TestCaptureInstallsEveryPayloadBlob`: every raw-manifest entry's blob present in the store after `Capture`; same assertion added to the crash replay in `TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates` | `TestCaptureInstallsEveryPayloadBlob` FAILs under `N-payload-install-blob-b` (blob-b sealed, never installed) | `mutants/run1/N-payload-install-blob-b.log`, `mutants/run2/N-payload-install-blob-b.log` (`# exit=1`, `--- FAIL: TestCaptureInstallsEveryPayloadBlob`) |\n38|| P2-α Row 8 (G2 pinned at the error only; target sink never inspected) | `TestProjectRefusesUnstable` now keeps its target sink and asserts it holds zero blobs on the archive path | Same test FAILs under `N-archive-emits-receipt` (archive manifest written to the target sink before the refusal) | `mutants/run1/N-archive-emits-receipt.log`, `mutants/run2/N-archive-emits-receipt.log` (`# exit=1`) |\n39|| P2-α Row 2 (every symlink/FIFO row `Required: true`) | New `TestCaptureRefusesOptionalSymlinkedIntermediate` (`Required: false` behind a symlinked intermediate refuses naming the member) + `TestCaptureRefusesOptionalFIFO` | `TestCaptureRefusesOptionalSymlinkedIntermediate` FAILs under `N-optional-blocked-ancestor` (optional-absent branch drops the `blockedAncestor` guard, seals `plan_optional_absent`) | `mutants/run1/N-optional-blocked-ancestor.log`, `mutants/run2/N-optional-blocked-ancestor.log` (`# exit=1`) |\n40|| P2-α Row 9 (unreadable-at-post class had no row) | New `TestCaptureRaceUnreadableAtPost`: member grows past `MaxSingleBytes` between walk and post — same regular key, cannot be re-read — race refuses naming it | Same test FAILs under `N-post-fallback-captured` (post falls back to the captured hash, seals stable) | `mutants/run1/N-post-fallback-captured.log`, `mutants/run2/N-post-fallback-captured.log` (`# exit=1`) |\n41|| P2-α Row 5 / P3-ε (excluded unknown unpinned) | New `TestCaptureOptionalAbsentUnknownMakesRawIncomplete`: optional absent `unknown` plan member seals excluded (`plan_optional_absent`), drives `raw_complete=false`, blocks `AdmitForTarget(maximal_safe)`, admits `strict_exact` | Same test FAILs under `N-clonebundle-unknown-excluded` — plant in `internal/clonebundle/capturebuild.go` (`hasUnknownClass` ignores excluded), killer here | `mutants/run1/N-clonebundle-unknown-excluded.log`, `mutants/run2/N-clonebundle-unknown-excluded.log` (`# exit=1`) |\n42|| P3-γ (false \"would fail closed under a reorder\" justification, 4 places) | Sealed the measured post digest for `post_capture_digest` (`capture.go`); reworded the bound in the `sealAndPublish` doc comment, `TRACEABILITY.md`, `LOGBOOK.md`, and here; strengthened `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt` to assert the race refusal literal (an early seal now refuses with a seal error, so the ordering killer reddens on the wrong error and on any receipt) | `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt` FAILs under `N-race-order-project` (`misses \"source mutated during capture\"`); `TestCaptureRaceSealsNoManifest` FAILs under `N-race-order-capture` (raw manifest published) | `mutants/run1/N-race-order-project.log` (`--- FAIL`, seal error misses the race literal), `mutants/run1/N-race-order-capture.log` |\n43|| P3-δ (`N-workspace-cwd` measured the message) | Harness note reworded: defence-in-depth, message-keyed — the landed relative-path grammar still refuses; the killer reddens on the missing `escapes the workspace root` literal | `TestCheckpointWorkspaceRefusesEscape` (unchanged killer, still KILLED) | `mutants/run1/N-workspace-cwd.log` |\n44|| P3-ε′ (leak rows killed by the builder, not the scan) | Shipped `N-excluded-orphan-blob` (add-write): excluded bytes installed as an orphan blob with no manifest entry and no log line | `TestCaptureExcludesSecrets` FAILs on the blob scan under the plant | `mutants/run1/N-excluded-orphan-blob.log`, `mutants/run2/N-excluded-orphan-blob.log` (`# exit=1`) |\n45|| P3-ζ′ (fidelity vocabulary spelled twice) | Recorded as an explicit bound: `sessadapter` owns an unexported table, this package a closed switch; the Final leaf unifies or exports one owner (`project.go` comment, `TRACEABILITY.md`, matrix, results) | Bound, not a gate: no killer (both spellings pinned by their own suites) | `internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md` stated bounds |\n46|\n47|## Inherited advisories (predecessor verdict rev6)\n48|\n49|- P3-ε (`hasUnknownClass` pinned only for INCLUDED unknown):\n50|  **CLOSED here.** `TestCaptureOptionalAbsentUnknownMakesRawIncomplete`\n51|  drives build derivation (`raw_complete=false`), decode, and\n52|  `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` at this leaf's projection entry\n53|  through `Capture` + `AdmitForTarget`; `N-clonebundle-unknown-excluded`\n54|  (plant in clonebundle, killer here) is KILLED 2/2.\n55|- P3-ζ (lone-surrogate member unpinned at `validText`): **DEFERRED to\n56|  TASK-260830-32ypr2.** This leaf owns no title/text admission site\n57|  (capture keys route through `SanitizeNativeKey`'s own UTF-8 gate,\n58|  never `validText`); the Final leaf owns projection fidelity over\n59|  session/event text and carries the row + harness row.\n60|- P3-η (`EncodeNativeIdentity` standalone admits what decoding\n61|  refuses): **PARTIAL — entry pinned here, standalone contract\n62|  deferred.** `TestCaptureRefusesInvalidSourceIdentity` drives five\n63|  undecodable identities (513-character native ID, kind `bogus`,\n64|  zero workspace ID, `native\\xff`, `/abs/native`) through `Capture`\n65|  and proves the entry re-validates via the landed `IdentityDigest`\n66|  (no manifest published); the `CaptureRequest.SourceIdentity` doc\n67|  states the re-validation. The standalone-entry bound (re-decode\n68|  inside the entry or an explicit pre-validated-identity contract)\n69|  belongs to the clonebundle owner or the Final leaf.\n70|\n71|## AC coverage: 17 of 17 rows driven and measured\n72|\n73|See `TASK-260830-2g5be6_conformance-matrix.md`: every row names its\n74|production call site and driving test, and every row's narrowing\n75|reddens its killer in the shipped battery (run twice). Ratio:\n76|**17 of 17 AC rows driven and measured at the member level** (rev1\n77|claimed 17 of 17 driven; the reviewer measured 12 of 17 at the\n78|member level; the five gaps above are now closed with executed\n79|kills).\n80|\n81|## Validation reran (this run, final tree)\n82|\n83|- Commands 1-3 (gofmt check, build, vet): exit 0 (`cmd01.log`,\n84|  `cmd02.log`, `cmd03.log`)\n85|- Command 4 (`go test ./... -count=1`): exit 0, 39 packages ok,\n86|  zero FAIL (`cmd04.log`)\n87|- Command 5 (race gate): exit 0 in four bounded package groups\n88|  a/b/c/d (10+10+10+9 packages ok, zero `DATA RACE`, zero FAIL)\n89|  instead of one 25m call, per the headless time bound\n90|  (`cmd05a.log` … `cmd05d.log`; `sessquery` 302.9s in group D)\n91|- Command 6 (cover gate): exit 0 in two bounded groups (20+19\n92|  packages ok, zero FAIL) (`cmd06a.log`, `cmd06b.log`;\n93|  `internal/clonesnap` 87.3% statements)\n94|- Commands 7-20 (fuzz smokes, 14 targets): exit 0 (`cmd07.log` …\n95|  `cmd20.log`)\n96|- Command 21 (`tracecheck`): exit 0, bindings=68, clauses 49/569 —\n97|  unchanged, `internal/traceability` untouched (`cmd21.log`)\n98|- Command 22 (`cata