{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c815","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2d0-7ac7-7f03-8c97-ccb0ee9decb3"},"sequence":613,"recorded_at":1780531400001221,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.started","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b2d2-5346-7ec2-a378-069f3503ca03"},"task_id":"01a0b2d2-5346-7ec2-a378-069f3503ca03","event":{"kind":"started","task_id":"01a0b2d2-5346-7ec2-a378-069f3503ca03","span_id":"03e02b6e7eb83fd9"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c817","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2d0-7ac7-7f03-8c97-ccb0ee9decb3"},"sequence":614,"recorded_at":1780531400001223,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b2d2-5324-73b1-a410-955808ac2e0a"},"task_id":"01a0b2d2-5324-73b1-a410-955808ac2e0a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b2d2-5324-73b1-a410-955808ac2e0a","chunk":"Read text file `internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Native Capture Clause Coverage (TASK-260830-2g5be6)\n2|\n3|Owner: `internal/clonesnap`. Authority:\n4|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1\n5|(the pinned sections are byte-identical to v0.6.0).\n6|The Story's FINAL leaf carries the `internal/traceability` registry\n7|bindings and re-pin; this file is the second-leaf clause record.\n8|\n9|## Why this package captures instead of clonebundle\n10|\n11|The predecessor leaf (`internal/clonebundle`) owns the capture\n12|contracts: the closed manifest/boundary/blob/identity shapes, their\n13|builders and decoders. This package owns the capture OPERATION over\n14|a real on-disk provider store: the contained walk, item\n15|classification, boundary construction from measured evidence, the\n16|source-race check, the workspace checkpoint, and target admission.\n17|Every artifact emitted here is produced through the landed\n18|clonebundle builders (`BuildRawObjectManifest`,\n19|`BuildCaptureManifest`, `SanitizeNativeKey`, `CheckDigestsEqual`,\n20|`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete`,\n21|`InstallRawBlob`, `VerifyDescriptorAgreement`,\n22|`DecodeWorkspaceBinding`, `IdentityDigest`) and re-decoded by the\n23|landed decoders before it is published or returned; no second\n24|manifest, boundary, blob, or identity model exists here.\n25|\n26|## Landed-owner reuse\n27|\n28|| Scope | Owner | Use |\n29||---|---|---|\n30|| Manifest/boundary/item/identity shapes | `internal/clonebundle` | all Build/Decode/Refuse entries above |\n31|| Store containment (openat-relative Guard walk) | `internal/secprim` | every payload open via `Guard.Open` from a verified root handle; member grammar via `CheckMemberPath` |\n32|| Durable writes (no-replace, fsync, verify) | `internal/localstore` | payload blobs via `InstallRawBlob`, manifests and receipts via `ObjectStore.PutBlob` |\n33|| Blob Descriptor shape and identity | `internal/canonicaljson` | `CalculateObjectIdentity` plus local claim comparisons; never the attesting entry |\n34|| Capture class vocabulary | `internal/clonebundle` | `ValidCaptureClass` (mirrors the `sessadapter` plan vocabulary) |\n35|| String measure, digests, UUIDv7, paths | `internal/environ`, `internal/scalar` | `StringLength`, `ParseDigest`, `ParseUUIDv7`, `ParseRelativePath`, `ParseAbsolutePath` |\n36|| Canonical bytes | `internal/canonicaljson` | `Canonicalize` for the workspace binding and the admission receipt |\n37|\n38|## Clause map\n39|\n40|| Pinned clause | Production entry | Test |\n41||---|---|---|\n42|| 13.14.1 Raw Manifest from real bytes: sorted unique entries, sanitized key, class, byte count, blob ID, descriptor ID | `Capture`, `BuildRawObjectManifest` (landed) | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureIsByteIdenticalAcrossRuns` |\n43|| 13.14.1 Capture Manifest from real evidence: basis, boundary, items, excluded classes, derived raw_complete | `Capture`, `BuildCaptureManifest` (landed) | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureOptionalAbsentSealsExcluded` |\n44|| 13.14.1 CaptureItem 9-class vocabulary + included/excluded content rule | `checkPlan` via `ValidCaptureClass`, `sealAndPublish` | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureRefusesMysteryPlanClass` |\n45|| 13.14.1 always-excluded classes never included; bytes never reach blob/manifest/log/error | `excludedClass` (never opened) | `TestCaptureExcludesSecrets` (one fixture member per class, full-artifact scan) |\n46|| 13.14.1 unknown makes raw_complete false and blocks maximal_safe | `sealAndPublish`, `AdmitForTarget` via `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` | `TestCaptureUnknownMakesRawIncomplete` (included), `TestCaptureOptionalAbsentUnknownMakesRawIncomplete` (excluded, P3-ε), `TestProjectMaximalSafeRequiresComplete`, `TestProjectMaximalSafeAdmitsComplete`, `TestProjectStrictExactAdmitsUnknown` |\n47|| 13.14.1 stable boundary: closed proof kind, generation, equal pre/post digests, idle facts | `sealAndPublish` via `buildBoundary` (landed) | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureImmutableSnapshotProof` |\n48|| 13.14.1 size equality is never proof | `checkSourceRace` via `CheckDigestsEqual` | `TestCaptureRaceChangedByte` (equal-size differing bytes refuse) |\n49|| 13.14.1 unstable_archive: generation, pre/post, source_not_quiescent, explicit ack, target forbidden; core-created, archive-only | `raceOutcome`, `sealAndPublish` (`Core: true`) | `TestCaptureArchiveSealsUnstable` (literal kind/reason/ack/forbidden assertions) |\n50|| 13.14.1 G2 rejects unstable | `AdmitForTarget` via `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestProjectRefusesUnstable` (refusal + target sink empty), `TestProjectRefusesUnstableDirect` |\n51|| Source race detected before projection: changed byte/size, appended record, replaced file, unreadable at post | `walkAndMeasure`, `measurePost`, `gateSourceRace` | `TestCaptureRaceChangedByte/ChangedSize/AppendedRecord/ReplacedFile/RemovedFile/UnreadableAtPost` |\n52|| Race gate precedes any seal or projection output | `Capture`, `CaptureAndProject` (ORDER-PIN) | `TestCaptureRaceSealsNoManifest` (no manifest published), `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt` (race refusal, not a seal error, + target sink empty) |\n53|| 13.14.1 WorkspaceBinding from real state: normalized cwd, sorted unique fingerprints[0..128], branch, head/index/tree | `CheckpointWorkspace` via `DecodeWorkspaceBinding` (landed) | `TestCheckpointWorkspaceSealsObservedState`, `...RelativeCwd`, `...RootCwd`, refusal rows |\n54|| 13.14.1 no member grants filesystem authority | `workspaceCwdRelative` | `TestCheckpointWorkspaceRefusesEscape/DotSegments/MissingCwd/FileCwd/SymlinkRoot` |\n55|| 13.14.1 source basis ax_session / external_native | `Capture` via `buildSourceBasis` (landed) | `TestCaptureExternalNativeBasis`, `TestCaptureRefusesMixedSourceBasis/UnknownBasisKind/UnsanitizedExternalRef` |\n56|| SourceIdentity re-validated at the entry (P3-η, this leaf) | `Capture` via `IdentityDigest` (landed, re-decodes) | `TestCaptureRefusesInvalidSourceIdentity` (overlong ID, bogus kind, zero workspace, bad UTF-8, absolute ref; no manifest published) |\n57|| 10.2 fsync + verify + atomic install before publishing a referencing record | `InstallRawBlob`, `PutBlob` (landed) | `TestCaptureInstallsEveryPayloadBlob` (every entry's blob present), crash replay assertion, `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestProjectIsIdempotent` |\n58|| 10.2 logs record digest, size, media type only | `CaptureLog` (no byte parameter) | `TestCaptureLogRecordsDigestsOnly`, `TestCaptureExcludesSecrets` (log scan) |\n59|| 10.2 Blob Descriptor: sorted contiguous non-overlapping chunks from zero covering size; index from zero by one; empty = size zero, no chunks | `BuildBlobDescriptor` via `CalculateObjectIdentity` + `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` | `TestCaptureEmptyMemberSealsEmptyBlob`, `TestCaptureMultiChunkMember`, `TestCaptureDescriptorAgreementEndToEnd` |\n60|| 10.2 oversized blob fails with capability_unavailable before a partial manifest | `openMember` limit gate | `TestCaptureRefusesOversizedMember`, `TestCaptureRefusesSparseOversizedMember`, `TestDefaultMaxSingleBytesIs128GiB` |\n61|| 7.8 fidelity profiles strict_exact\\|maximal_safe\\|compact\\|messages_only | `AdmitForTarget`, `BuildAdmissionReceipt` | `TestProjectAdmitsStableEveryProfile`, `TestProjectRefusesUnknownProfile` |\n62|| 1.6 string measure in characters | `workspaceNullableText` via `environ.StringLength` | `TestCheckpointWorkspaceMultibyteBranch` |\n63|| Containment: symlinked intermediate and FIFO refuse before any payload open, member named; no escape past the root | `openMember` via `secprim.Guard` | `TestCaptureRefusesSymlinkedIntermediate/OptionalSymlinkedIntermediate/TrailingSymlink/FIFO/OptionalFIFO/DirectoryMember/ParentPlanKey` |\n64|| Unplanned members refuse; one item per plan candidate | `planMemberClass` | `TestCaptureRefusesUnplannedMember/PrefixSibling/RequiredMissing/DuplicatePlanKey` |\n65|\n66|## Durability\n67|\n68|This package performs durable writes only through\n69|`localstore.ObjectStore.PutBlob`: payload blobs (via the landed\n70|`InstallRawBlob`), manifest blobs, and admission receipt blobs. The\n71|landed discipline (stage, fsync, size/digest verification, atomic\n72|no-replace install, directory fsync, quarantine on mismatch) carries\n73|the crash semantics; this package adds the publish ORDER (payloads,\n74|then raw, then capture, then receipt) and the hooks that pin it.\n75|`TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates` kills a live capture between\n76|the raw and capture publishes and proves the replay converges with\n77|byte-identical manifests; `TestProjectIsIdempotent` proves a\n78|replayed capture verifies and reuses every blob and publishes no\n79|half-written manifest (every manifest blob re-decodes). No second\n80|write path exists in this package.\n81|\n82|## Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived)\n83|\n84|- No `ax` CLI, no provider process, no network: the store is a\n85|  fixture directory. Section 7.8 capture-plan/capture/normalize\n86|  operation wiring stays owned by `sessadapter`; this package\n87|  consumes plan keys and classes, it does not speak the adapter\n88|  protocol.\n89|- The sealed stable proof carries the two measured source digests\n90|  (pre and post): the race gate proved them equal before the seal\n91|  ran, so on the stable path the sealed bytes equal either\n92|  measurement, and the landed builder refuses unequal digests.\n93|  The ordering mutants (`N-race-order-capture`,\n94|  `N-race-order-project`) move the gate after the seal and the\n95|  killers redden on the published manifests and receipt, which\n96|  proves the gate precedes the seal either way the digests seal.\n97|- Excluded-class bytes are never opened, so a changed byte at\n98|  equal size inside an excluded member is below the detection\n99|  floor: presence, shape, and size changes still race. Excluded\n100|  bytes cannot affect capture output, and the never-open rule is\n101|  what the leak suite proves.\n102|- Enumeration observes names through path strings; every OPEN\n103|  descends from the verified root handle through the Guard. A\n104|  sub-walk transient swap restored before the post measurement is\n105|  below the detection floor (no filesystem snapshot); any\n106|  persistent change races, and blob integrity of the read bytes is\n107|  guaranteed by the install-time verification regardless.\n108|- Optional included-class candidates absent from the store seal as\n109|  excluded rows with reason `plan_optional_absent`; required ones\n110|  refuse. Required-ness for excluded classes is inert (presence is\n111|  irrelevant to bytes that are never opened).\n112|- `MaxSingleBytes` mirrors the Section 7.8 `ResourceLimits`\n113|  per-object bound; zero selects the Section 10.2 default of\n114|  137438953472 (32768 chunks of 4194304 bytes). The sparse\n115|  oversized row pins the default end to end without reading 128\n116|  GiB.\n117|- The admission receipt (`urn:ax:internal:clonesnap-admission-receipt`\n118|  1.0.0) proves target admission and race-before-projection\n119|  ordering only. Projection planning past admission, per-kind\n120|  event payload registries, and `strict_exact`/`compact`/\n121|  `messages_only` planning semantics are the final leaf's and the\n122|  normalization sibling's.\n123|- `internal/traceability` registry bindings and digest re-pin\n124|  (Story FINAL leaf).\n125|- The four-profile fidelity vocabulary is spelled twice:\n126|  `sessadapter` owns an unexported table and this package owns a\n127|  closed switch (P3-ζ′). The FINAL leaf unifies or exports one\n128|  owner; both spellings are pinned by their own suites today.\n129|- `EncodeNativeIdentity` standalone trusts the caller for bounds,\n130|  vocabulary, and the workspace ID (P3-η remainder): this leaf's\n131|  seal path re-decodes through the landed callers\n132|  (`sealAndPublish` calls `IdentityDigest` directly and\n133|  `BuildCaptureManifest` re-decodes the source identity\n134|  internally), pinned by `TestCaptureRefusesInvalidSourceIdentity`.\n135|  The standalone-entry bound (re-decode inside the entry or an\n136|  explicit pre-validated-identity contract) belongs to the\n137|  clonebundle owner or the Final leaf.\n138|- The lone-surrogate member at the shared `validText` gate (P3-ζ)\n139|  is not exercised here: this leaf owns no title/text admission\n140|  site. Deferred to the Final leaf, which owns projection\n141|  fidelity over session/event text.","final_result":true}}}
