{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca9b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2d0-7ac7-7f03-8c97-ccb0ee9decb3"},"sequence":936,"recorded_at":1780531400001867,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b2d4-1711-7ad0-b689-fb62ac907675"},"task_id":"01a0b2d4-1711-7ad0-b689-fb62ac907675","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b2d4-1711-7ad0-b689-fb62ac907675","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-22-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git fetch origin main 2>&1 | tail -n 3; echo \\\"origin/main: $(git rev-parse origin/main)\\\"; echo \\\"HEAD: $(git rev-parse HEAD)\\\"; git log --oneline origin/main -3 2>&1\\necho ===\\nhead -n 60 LOGBOOK.md\\necho ===README-SECTION===\\ngrep -n \\\"clonesnap\\\" README.md | head\",\n  \"description\": \"Check origin state and logbook head\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"From github.com:relux-works/agent-session-manager\\n * branch            main       -> FETCH_HEAD\\norigin/main: c3aae73df906df1b5aa962c7bc3c16437dd920fa\\nHEAD: 2f844bb49702a860c1199a6a2a0ca6a5cc878197\\nc3aae73 Record STORY-260830-4qojoz board state\\n978e200 STORY-260830-4qojoz: STORY-260830-4qojoz: mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation\\na12d1bd BUG-260918-354b03: derive the smoke deadline from the real clock\\n===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2g5be6 — native capture and source-race check (second leaf)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/clonesnap` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture operation over a real fixture store — contained walk (`secprim` Guard opens, symlink-intermediate/FIFO/dir refusals naming the member), nine-class classification with always-excluded bytes never opened, Capture Boundary from measured evidence (stable proof or core-created `unstable_archive`), a source-race gate comparing content digests before any seal, workspace checkpoint + source head from observed state, Section 10.2 descriptors (empty/multi-chunk) with `capability_unavailable` past 128 GiB, and target admission (`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete`) emitting an admission receipt. Every manifest seals through the landed `clonebundle` builders and re-decodes before publish; every byte installs through `localstore` no-replace.\\n- ORDERING (the task's named check): the sealed stable proof carries the two measured source digests (pre and post) — the gate proved them equal before the seal ran, so the sealed bytes equal either measurement — and the `N-race-order-capture` / `N-race-order-project` mutants prove the gate precedes the seal and the receipt. Changed byte/size, appended record, replaced/removed file, and unreadable-at-post each refuse or seal `unstable_archive` with `source_not_quiescent`, never silently stable.\\n- EVIDENCE: package suite green (positives, full refusal table, 4-class leak scan over blobs/manifests/logs/errors, digest-only log assertions, every-payload-blob-installed assertion after Capture and after the crash replay, target-sink-empty assertion on the archive path, real-SIGKILL crash test with replay convergence + clean-run byte equality, idempotent triple-project); 32 narrowing + 2 add-write rows KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, one raw log per plant with subprocess exit, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including the token-preserving prefix mutant killed by the behavioral Capture entry and the cross-package P3-ε row (plant in clonebundle, killer here). No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- INHERITED (rev2 rework): P3-ε CLOSED here (excluded unknown drives `raw_complete=false` and blocks `maximal_safe` at this leaf's projection entry, test + cross-package harness row); P3-ζ DEFERRED to TASK-260830-32ypr2 (no title/text admission site in this leaf); P3-η PARTIAL — this leaf's entry re-validation pinned by test, the standalone `EncodeNativeIdentity` contract deferred to the clonebundle owner or the final leaf. P3-γ sealed the measured post digest; P3-δ reworded as defence-in-depth; P3-ε′ orphan-blob row shipped; P3-ζ′ fidelity duplication recorded as a bound.\\n- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): no `ax` CLI/provider process/network (fixture store); Section 7.8 operation wiring stays `sessadapter`; projection planning past admission is the final leaf's; excluded-byte equal-size changes are below the detection floor (never opened by design); sub-walk transient swaps restored before post-measure are below the floor (no fs snapshot). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- AC: 17 of 17 rows driven through production entries by named tests and measured at the member level — every row's narrowing reddens its killer (matrix in `TASK-260830-2g5be6_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-24z2b3 — clone bundle + canonical session/event types (first leaf)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/clonebundle` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture contracts over the landed owners — Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 (Capture Items, Source Basis, Capture Boundary, core-derived `raw_complete`), Canonical Session 1.0.0 + Actors, Canonical Event 1.0.0 (Source Evidence, raw refs, content blocks), NativeIdentity/WorkspaceBinding, immutable generations — plus Section 10.2 descriptor agreement and no-replace install via `localstore`. Every Build entry is byte-identical for identical inputs; every Decode entry enforces the closed shape. Row-21 exclusion allowlist (`hosttrust` matchers) enforced at raw-entry and capture-item construction with per-class negatives.\\n- OWNERSHIP: `canonicaljson` keeps its `rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape` rows (that table's census pins every row); this package is the validating owner and reuses `Canonicalize` (byte transform), `CalculateObjectIdentity` plus local claim comparisons (blobs; never the attesting `VerifyObjectIdentity` entry — only the test fixture calls it — per the provhost no-attestation bound), `sessadapter.DecodeTuple`, the `environ` scalar gate set via delegating wrappers, `scalar`, `hosttrust`, and `localstore.PutBlob`. No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- EVIDENCE: package suite green (87.1% statements), 66 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, one raw log per plant with subprocess exit, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`); `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` + `TestInstallRawBlobRefusals` prove the localstore delegation (double install agrees; forged claim, short/long/tampered bytes refuse); durability itself is the landed localstore discipline (purity bound for this package: no second write path). README package section added with test commands and no capability claim.\\n- REV3 (rework of review RUN-260917-c05bc8): P1-a descriptor identity linked to the entry at build + evidence verification; P1-b AX number model + nested-duplicate refusal on extension values at build + decode; P2-f/P2-a environ gate adoption with the character string measure; P2-b/P2-c decode-side negatives for every surviving row + verifier/install negatives with per-plant logs; P2-d duplicate raw keys refused; P2-e identity re-decode before hashing; P3-b content XOR enforced; P3-c one-per-plan-candidate refused at build; P3-a sanitizer hardened with the exact bound stated; P3-d/P3-e harness rows fixed; P3-f/g/h hygiene. Finding-by-finding table in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md`.\\n- REV4 (rework of review RUN-260917-62d051; base refreshed 888ae3d→2fc6d50, authority now SPEC.v0.7.0 with byte-identical pinned sections): P1-c payload value model enforced for every event kind at build + decode with exact-int64 sealing (sealed bytes never round/collapse); P2-α one extension value-fault row per admission site (17 rows + 17 narrowing plants); P2-β decode duplicate-entry row; P2-γ duplicate plan keys refused; P3 null-content XOR, refusal-detail fixes, input_blocked/-(2^53)/U+2029/payload-top-dup/external-null-parent rows, EncodeNativeIdentity validation, N-main-count split, dead code removed, census version/not-array/maxima/overflow rows with the remainder stated as defense-in-depth. Finding-by-finding table in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md`.\\n- REV5 (rework of review RUN-260917-ab25c8; no base move, still 2fc6d50; every rev3 finding verified fixed, scope one P2 + four P3): P2-δ shared valid-UTF-8 text gate at every Build string admission (title, actor name/model, native_type, reason codes, exclusion_reason, generation, extension keys/values at any depth) plus `EncodeNativeIdentity` sanitizing both native keys before marshaling — invalid UTF-8 and lone surrogates refuse instead of sealing as U+FFFD, and the \\\"native\\\\xff\\\" vs \\\"native\\\\xfe\\\" collision pair both refuse; `TestBuildTextMustBeValidUTF8` (22 rows + collision pair) asserts the sealed bytes carry no U+FFFD, killed by the N-text-utf8 narrowing plant. P3: evidence archive rebuilt from a task-scoped dir (no foreign artifacts, no `__pycache__`); `-0`-only TRACEABILITY sentence first-hand verified (`+1`/`01` refuse \\\"not a JSON object\\\", `-0` passes the gate); build reason-duplicate row + N-reason-codes-dup-build plant; producer checklist rows only. Finding-by-finding table in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md`.\\n- REV5b (completion run: rev5 Change Request construction failed at command 6 on the trunk resumesmoke time-bomb, not on the candidate): base refreshed 2fc6d50→a12d1bd via `refresh-candidate` (trunk BUG-260918-354b03 fix); audit: the refresh had carried the old `support_test.go` as uncommitted delta — trunk content restored by hand — and a stray `zz_debug_test.go` scratch probe was removed; candidate code unchanged; the full 27-command suite, package suite, P3-b probe, and mutant battery were re-executed on the new base with fresh logs.\\n- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): per-kind event payload fact registries past the envelope (which facts a kind may carry; the §1.6 value model on every payload member is enforced here); `maximal_safe` planning past the refusal gate; G2 admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`; Section 7.8 operation wiring (stays `sessadapter`). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- AC: 18 of 18 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n\\n### TASK-260917-10k118: reconstructed the reviewed v0.7.0 adoption on trunk 7efe385 (STORY-260916-3uqbwq unlandable, accepted CRs frozen)\\n- METHOD: true pin delta is `git diff e4e3e88 9cb5dd4` (10 files) — the exported 238-file patch diffs unrelated tips and would revert five landed stories, so it was used as transport only; rev3 candidate bytes applied (15 modified + 3 new) with the 5 trunk-merged files copied verbatim after diff-review (no trunk test lost, `task-board.config.json` untouched). All 19 machine-applied files `cmp`-identical to the rev3 bytes; ownership sha256 `2548870d…8a5070`, projection digest `c4cd46bf…53473f6` recomputed two independent ways.\\n- RE-VERIFIED (this session, fresh clone + production helpers): tag `d4abe46f…795b3` Good, peeled `32b3f2ba…321834`, SPEC blob `c4903e60…1ddd86` 1185291 bytes sha256 `c6b2fe64…89ddcf` byte-identical to `SPEC.v0.7.0.md`; lock 64/64 rows order- and set-identical to the §1.5 table (1 known order normalization); 65/65 bindings + 132/132 cases carried with 3 reviewed additions each; all 49 discharged clauses re-measured (unif