r 1.4.0/1.5.0 and manifest/probe 1.1.0 stay census-only (carrying 3.1.0 panics canonicaljson init — no Go shape validator yet — same init-panic rationale as error 1.4.0). +3 section bindings (13.1, 13.10, 14.1), +1 fixture (`pin:ax-launch-plan-request-v1`), gaps updated for 5.1/7.3/7.4/7.5/appendix-d with story owners; 48 carried clause lines re-measured against SPEC.v0.7.0.md (uniform +20/+79/+185/+281/+392 shifts, every excerpt verbatim, no ID shifts).\\n- OWNERS: all 7 launch-plan clause areas name implementing EPIC-260916-18uelk stories with unevidenced coverage — 3fjjtn parsing/refusals (14.1, 13.1, contract), 2q85nu record embedding (5.1), 1kp1lx stdin/replay (7.5), 1ea7od plugin capability (7.3/7.4), 3aukw3 drift (13.10), 3ustb3 naming (13.1 split), vucwn0 vectors (fixture, appendix-d split). The source-derived AdoptedSections test requires 6/6 plus 2 split attributions and refuses each through VerifyAssignedSections.\\n- HISTORY: registry re-derived from the trunk-final v0.6.0 registry, carrying the five landed stories' 31 acceptance cases and 9 section bindings (2.2, 2.4, 5.3/5.4/5.5, 6.6, 7.7, 8, 10.6, 11.10.1–4, 13.12/13.13, 16.1) with re-measured clause lines; v0.6.0/v0.5.0 locks, registries, readers and historical tests byte-untouched versus trunk; the v0.7.0 inventory is identifier-equal to v0.6.0 (170 ids, same digest), so legacy verification derives both historical registries from the adopted lock. P3 closed: pin.go/specdoc.go consumer comments now true in the present tense; section:11.10.5 carried as a Disclosure owner (source evidence only, no implementation claim).\\n- FIGURES: contracts=64, normative section keys=36, acceptance cases=135, fixtures=33, historical contracts=55; bindings=68 (full=2, partial=6, sliver=4, unevidenced=52, unmeasured=4), unowned=7, discharged clauses=49/569. No launch-plan/stdin/caller_launch_plan/environment_drift/curator-run runtime claim anywhere.\\n- STATUS: implemented, tests green, ready for review; work left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for the handoff snapshot.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n- F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\n- F2 (MEASURED BOUND): an idle stream with zero traffic does NOT self-close within one second of revocation — `serveLoop` carries no background watchdog. The next dispatch fences in milliseconds and `WatchGeneration` reports the commit; recorded as a stated bound with log evidence, not a pass. Tailscale SSH and non-host lanes likewise bounded.\\n- F3: `os/exec.Cmd.Wait` called twice hangs the second caller forever — test cleanup consumes one `Wait` channel. The 8 MiB line cap is enforced twice (framing + decode), so the oversize mutant weakens both layers in one multi-file probe (harness extended for `(file, old, new)` triples). The Structured Error schema URN is `urn:ax:schema:error`; a drift vector with the wrong URN passed for the wrong reason until the mutant survived and exposed it.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 9 new narrowing probes, all killed by named `TestHostile*` vectors (same-family ALPN, dual-layer oversize, client rebind, rpc-contracts, error-version drift, truncated-dispatch ignore, snapshot integrity, correlation, static nonce); pre-existing 26 probes re-run green (neutral passed, client-cache documented SURVIVED). Per-plant logs/tables in the outcome tar.\\n- TRACEABILITY: `AC-HOST-001` registered over 20 suite tests; new `unevidenced` bindings for 11.10.1–11.10.4 + 16.1 with honest gaps (executed lanes vs stated bounds); 6.6/11.10 gaps refreshed; 11.10.5 stays unowned by design (no policy reader); digest re-pinned `e327bb08...`; report 102 cases / 61 bindings / 8 unowned / 17/487 clauses; README figures + tracecheck pins updated.\\n- AC: 7 of 7 hostile rows + 13 of 13 executed AC-HOST-001 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in the outcome evidence). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed. NOTE: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate` replay against `origin/main e4e3e88` fails on a LOGBOOK.md rebase conflict (missing replay resolution) — orchestrator-side integration issue, worktree untouched at `244a7dc`.\\n- 2026-09-17 rev3 on `fc67abd`: pin `d3eca906…`, report 132 cases / 65 bindings / 7 unowned / 49 of 535 clauses; harness denominator 24 prior + 9 new; refresh-candidate completed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2atgj4 — property-test the ownership reducer (final leaf)\\n\\n- SCOPE: executable proofs of the four story-pinned ownership invariants\\n  (union-order independence, loser preservation, clock non-authority,\\n===README-SECTION===\\n2426:[`internal/clonesnap`](internal/clonesnap) implements the Section\\n2437:[`internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md`](internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md)\\n2443:go test ./internal/clonesnap -count=1\\n2444:go test ./internal/clonesnap -count=1 -cover\\n2445:PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/clonesnap/testdata/mutant_harness.py\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 18908,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4727,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
