{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cf43","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2d0-7ac7-7f03-8c97-ccb0ee9decb3"},"sequence":1532,"recorded_at":1780531400003059,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b2d8-cd83-7032-b528-79d74deb274e"},"task_id":"01a0b2d8-cd83-7032-b528-79d74deb274e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b2d8-cd83-7032-b528-79d74deb274e","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-32-1\",\n  \"command\": \"mkdir -p /tmp/t2g5/ev/producer-evidence-TASK-260830-2g5be6/mutants/run1 /tmp/t2g5/ev/producer-evidence-TASK-260830-2g5be6/mutants/run2\\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/clonesnap/testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir /tmp/t2g5/ev/producer-evidence-TASK-260830-2g5be6/mutants/run1 2>&1 | tee /tmp/t2g5/ev/producer-evidence-TASK-260830-2g5be6/mutants-run1.log | tail -n 50; echo HARNESS_EXIT:${PIPESTATUS[0]}\",\n  \"description\": \"Run full mutant battery run 1\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"ok: N-contain-trailing: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Stands forged bytes in for the Guard open of exactly link-escape; every other member still opens through the Guard.\\nok: N-contain-intermediate: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Stands forged bytes in for the Guard open of exactly link-escape/file; every other member still opens through the Guard.\\nok: N-fifo: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Stands forged bytes in for the Guard open of exactly stash-fifo; every other member still opens through the Guard.\\nok: N-unplanned: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly store/zz-extra past the plan gate as durable_payload; every other unplanned key still refuses.\\nok: N-plan-prefix: KILLED (want KILLED) :: TOKEN-PRESERVING: the lookup still compares against the planned keys but admits prefix matches, so store/blob-a-evil rides on store/blob-a. The killer drives the full Capture entry.\\nok: N-plan-order: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly duplicate plan keys; unsorted keys still refuse with the plan detail.\\nok: N-plan-sanitize: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly one UUIDv7 plan key past the sanitizer; every other unsanitized key still refuses. Token preserved.\\nok: N-plan-class: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly class mystery past the vocabulary gate; every other unknown class still refuses.\\nok: N-exclude-credential: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly credential rows as included; the other three always-excluded classes still exclude.\\nok: N-exclude-machine-auth: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly machine_auth rows as included; the other three always-excluded classes still exclude.\\nok: N-exclude-runtime-state: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly runtime_state rows as included; the other three always-excluded classes still exclude.\\nok: N-exclude-transient-lock: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly transient_lock rows as included; the other three always-excluded classes still exclude.\\nok: N-required: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly store/must-have past the required-absent refusal; every other required-absent candidate still refuses.\\nok: N-optional: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Refuses exactly the optional-absent store/maybe that must seal as excluded; every other optional-absent still seals.\\nok: N-race-narrow: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Ignores exactly races naming store/blob-a; races on every other member still refuse.\\nok: N-race-order-capture: KILLED (want KILLED) :: ORDERING: seals and publishes before the race gate; the killer reddens on the published manifests and the non-nil result.\\nok: N-race-order-project: KILLED (want KILLED) :: ORDERING: seals, admits and emits before the race gate; the early seal refuses with a seal error instead of the race refusal, so the killer reddens on the wrong error. Killed by the seal error message, not by a sink assertion — the seal half is pinned by N-race-order-project-seal.\\nok: N-race-order-project-seal: KILLED (want KILLED) :: ORDERING at the projection entry: seals and publishes the raw manifest BEFORE the race gate while preserving the race error (the stable capture-manifest seal fails closed on unequal digests, so no receipt is emitted); the killer reddens on the sealed raw manifest in the capture store.\\nok: N-explicit: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Seals unstable output without acknowledgement for exactly generation-9; every other generation still refuses.\\nok: N-g2: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly generation-9 unstable archives to the target branch; every other unstable still refuses.\\nok: N-maximal: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly the three-item unknown manifest to maximal_safe; unknown manifests of every other size still refuse.\\nok: N-fidelity: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly profile ultra; every other unknown profile still refuses.\\nok: N-oversize: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly 11-byte members past the size bound; every other oversized member still refuses.\\nok: N-descriptor-empty: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Seals exactly empty payloads with a zero-size chunk; every non-empty payload still seals clean chunks.\\nok: N-descriptor-offset: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Shifts exactly the second chunk off contiguity; single-chunk descriptors still seal.\\nok: N-workspace-cwd: KILLED (want KILLED) :: P3-δ (defence-in-depth, message-keyed): admits exactly /outside-workspace past the line-120 escape check while the landed relative-path grammar still refuses it; the killer reddens on the missing 'escapes the workspace root' literal, not on admission.\\nok: N-workspace-fingerprints: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly duplicate fingerprints; unsorted fingerprints still refuse with the checkpoint detail.\\nok: N-log-leak: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Leaks exactly store/blob-a payload bytes into the log; every other member still logs digests only.\\nok: N-hook-crash: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Skips the crash-boundary hook for exactly the crash generation; the child exits clean and the parent misses its SIGKILL.\\nok: N-payload-install-blob-b: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Seals exactly store/blob-b into the raw manifest without installing its blob; every other member still installs. The killer scans the store for every referenced blob.\\nok: N-archive-emits-receipt: KILLED (want KILLED) :: P3 row 8 (add-write, not a narrowing): writes the archive capture manifest into the TARGET sink before the G2 refusal; the killer asserts the target sink is empty, not only that admission refused.\\nok: N-optional-blocked-ancestor: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Seals an optional member behind a symlinked intermediate as plan_optional_absent instead of routing it to the Guard refusal; required members still route to the Guard.\\nok: N-post-fallback-captured: KILLED (want KILLED) :: A member unreadable at post time falls back to its captured hash instead of unknown content, so exactly the unreadable-at-post class misses the race; every re-readable member still compares fresh bytes.\\nok: N-clonebundle-unknown-excluded: KILLED (want KILLED) :: P3-ε: the plant lives in clonebundle (hasUnknownClass ignores excluded items) while the killer lives here — an excluded unknown item must still drive raw_complete=false and block maximal_safe at this leaf's projection entry.\\nok: N-excluded-orphan-blob: KILLED (want KILLED) :: P3-ε′ (add-write, not a narrowing): installs excluded bytes as an orphan blob with no manifest entry and no log line, so the killer's blob scan — not a builder refusal — must catch the leak.\\nok: N-unstable-seals-pre-as-post: KILLED (want KILLED) :: The unstable_archive form seals the PRE digest for post_capture_digest, so the archive manifest carries equal digests while flagged source_not_quiescent; the killer asserts the sealed digests equal the measured pre/post and the sealed generation equals the request generation.\\nok: N-unplanned-special: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Treats exactly the unplanned symlink stray-link as an intermediate, so it bypasses the 'not a plan candidate' refusal (and the early containment open) and the capture seals stable; every other unplanned key still refuses.\\nok: N-store-root-symlink: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Follows a trailing symlink at the store root for exactly link-root (every other symlinked root still refuses through the landed nofollow discipline); the killer asserts the refusal names the link and installs nothing.\\nok: N-excluded-size: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Exactly the excluded member store/token-cache contributes a constant size to the source record, so its size change between walk and post is missed; every other member still races on size.\\nok: N-plan-grammar-dotdot: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly store/../escape past the plan member-grammar gate (SanitizeNativeKey does not refuse parent segments, so this gate is the only one); every other escaping key still refuses.\\nok: N-required-blocked-ancestor: KILLED (want KILLED) :: A required member behind a symlinked intermediate refuses as 'required but absent' instead of reaching the Guard refusal that names the symlink escape; optional members still route to the Guard.\\nok: N-fingerprints-129: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Admits exactly 129 repository remote fingerprints past the [0..128] bound; the killer asserts the 'maximum is 128' refusal.\\nok: N-first-chunk-oversize: KILLED (want KILLED) :: Seals the first chunk of a multi-chunk blob at 4194305 bytes (chunk size bound uint53[1..4194304]); single-chunk descriptors still seal.\\nok: C-doc-comment: SURVIVED (want SURVIVED) :: Harmless control: a comment-only edit must survive.\\nHARNESS_EXIT:0\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8490,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2123,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
