{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d387","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b2d0-7ac7-7f03-8c97-ccb0ee9decb3"},"sequence":2078,"recorded_at":1780531400004151,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"6c09b2f8-d07d-42a7-92aa-11c55130fea2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b2ee-87f3-75a2-bcaf-84142e9abae7"},"task_id":"01a0b2ee-87f3-75a2-bcaf-84142e9abae7","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b2ee-87f3-75a2-bcaf-84142e9abae7","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-54-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git diff LOGBOOK.md | head -n 40; echo ===; git diff README.md | head -n 50\",\n  \"description\": \"Show inherited LOGBOOK and README diffs\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"diff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex ed67780..c59a9aa 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -3,6 +3,17 @@\\n > Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n > Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n \\n+## 2026-09-18\\n+\\n+### TASK-260830-2g5be6 — native capture and source-race check (second leaf)\\n+\\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/clonesnap` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture operation over a real fixture store — contained walk (`secprim` Guard opens, symlink-intermediate/FIFO/dir refusals naming the member), nine-class classification with always-excluded bytes never opened, Capture Boundary from measured evidence (stable proof or core-created `unstable_archive`), a source-race gate comparing content digests before any seal, workspace checkpoint + source head from observed state, Section 10.2 descriptors (empty/multi-chunk) with `capability_unavailable` past 128 GiB, and target admission (`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete`) emitting an admission receipt. Every manifest seals through the landed `clonebundle` builders and re-decodes before publish; every byte installs through `localstore` no-replace.\\n+- ORDERING (the task's named check): the sealed stable proof carries the two measured source digests (pre and post) — the gate proved them equal before the seal ran, so the sealed bytes equal either measurement — and the `N-race-order-capture` / `N-race-order-project` mutants prove the gate precedes the seal and the receipt. Changed byte/size, appended record, replaced/removed file, and unreadable-at-post each refuse or seal `unstable_archive` with `source_not_quiescent`, never silently stable.\\n+- EVIDENCE: package suite green (positives, full refusal table, 4-class leak scan over blobs/manifests/logs/errors, digest-only log assertions, every-payload-blob-installed assertion after Capture and after the crash replay, target-sink-empty assertion on the archive path, real-SIGKILL crash test with replay convergence + clean-run byte equality, idempotent triple-project); 32 narrowing + 2 add-write rows KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, one raw log per plant with subprocess exit, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including the token-preserving prefix mutant killed by the behavioral Capture entry and the cross-package P3-ε row (plant in clonebundle, killer here). No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n+- INHERITED (rev2 rework): P3-ε CLOSED here (excluded unknown drives `raw_complete=false` and blocks `maximal_safe` at this leaf's projection entry, test + cross-package harness row); P3-ζ DEFERRED to TASK-260830-32ypr2 (no title/text admission site in this leaf); P3-η PARTIAL — this leaf's entry re-validation pinned by test, the standalone `EncodeNativeIdentity` contract deferred to the clonebundle owner or the final leaf. P3-γ sealed the measured post digest; P3-δ reworded as defence-in-depth; P3-ε′ orphan-blob row shipped; P3-ζ′ fidelity duplication recorded as a bound.\\n+- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): no `ax` CLI/provider process/network (fixture store); Section 7.8 operation wiring stays `sessadapter`; projection planning past admission is the final leaf's; excluded-byte equal-size changes are below the detection floor (never opened by design); sub-walk transient swaps restored before post-measure are below the floor (no fs snapshot). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n+- AC: 17 of 17 rows driven through production entries by named tests and measured at the member level — every row's narrowing reddens its killer (matrix in `TASK-260830-2g5be6_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n+\\n ## 2026-09-17\\n \\n ### TASK-260830-24z2b3 — clone bundle + canonical session/event types (first leaf)\\n===\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex 3309f7b..909e642 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -2421,6 +2421,30 @@ go test ./internal/clonebundle -count=1 -cover\\n PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/clonebundle/testdata/mutant_harness.py\\n ```\\n \\n+## Native Capture and Source-Race Check\\n+\\n+[`internal/clonesnap`](internal/clonesnap) implements the Section\\n+13.14.1 native capture operation over a real on-disk provider store:\\n+a contained capture walk that produces the Clone Raw Object Manifest\\n+and Clone Capture Manifest from actual bytes, classifies every\\n+Capture Item, builds the Capture Boundary from measured evidence,\\n+detects source mutation before any projection output, checkpoints\\n+the workspace binding and source head, and admits stable captures to\\n+a target branch. Every payload open descends from a verified store\\n+handle through the `secprim` Guard; every manifest seals through the\\n+`clonebundle` builders; every byte installs through the `localstore`\\n+no-replace discipline. The clause map in\\n+[`internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md`](internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md)\\n+maps every pinned clause to its production entry and test, with the\\n+sibling-owned bounds stated. It adds no `ax` command, no `doctor`\\n+result, and no runtime capability claim.\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./internal/clonesnap -count=1\\n+go test ./internal/clonesnap -count=1 -cover\\n+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/clonesnap/testdata/mutant_harness.py\\n+```\\n+\\n ## Crash/Restart Outcome Gate\\n \\n [`internal/crashgate`](internal/crashgate) executes the Section 13.13\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5420,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1355,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
